WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.527
The amount column currently contains currency symbols, so we first remove the dollar sign from the text.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:12.072
Then we use the to numeric function to convert the cleaned values into numbers.

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:16.187
For the date column, we use the to date time function.

00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:19.657
Notice the errors option is set to coerce.

00:00:19.657 --> 00:00:27.212
This means invalid values are converted to missing values instead of causing the entire conversion to fail.

00:00:27.212 --> 00:00:33.181
That is useful because bad values become visible and can be handled explicitly.

00:00:33.631 --> 00:00:37.858
After conversion, always inspect the data types again.

00:00:37.858 --> 00:00:44.834
A transformation is not complete until you confirm that Pandas now stores the values in the form you expected.
